  "borough": "Enfield Council",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by virtue of its location within Flood Zone 3b which is an active flood plain, has failed to demonstrate that it would not result in increased potential for flooding on site and it could contribute to increased risk of flooding elsewhere. This would be detrimental to future occupiers of the property and those living in the surrounding area. The proposal is therefore contrary to the NPPF (2024), Policy SI 12 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP28 of Enfield's Core Policy (2010) and Policies DMD 59, DMD 60, DMD 61 and DMD 62 of Enfield's Development Management Document (2014).",
    "The proposed first-floor side-facing window serving Bedroom 5, by virtue of its position and the views it would have towards the rear garden of No. 11 Hartland Close, would result in an unacceptable loss of privacy to neighbouring occupiers. This impact is considered contrary to Section 12 of the National Planning Policy Framework (2024), Policies D4 and D5 of the London Plan (2021), Policy CP30 of Enfield's Core Strategy (2010), and Policy DMD 37 of the Development Management Document (2014)."
  ],
